Subject: src: bring the OpenVMS code paths up to date

The __VMS branch of utils.c still defined unique_name_passthrough() with
the two arguments it had before utils.h changed it to one, so utils.c did
not compile on VMS.  (On VMS, UNIQ_SEP is undefined on purpose: a file that
exists gets a new version instead of a .1, .2 suffix.)

warc.c's __VMS branch passes an RMS option ("fop=tmd", delete on close) to
fopen(), as ftp.c and utils.c do; include vms.h there too, which gives
those files the C RTL's variadic fopen() rather than gnulib's two-argument
replacement.

--- a/src/utils.c	2026-10-04 07:44:00.912413453 +0100
+++ b/src/utils.c	2026-10-04 07:44:00.934421275 +0100
@@ -708,7 +708,7 @@
    possible.
 */
 char *
-unique_name_passthrough (const char *file, bool allow_passthrough)
+unique_name_passthrough (const char *file)
 {
   /* Return the FILE itself, without modification, irregardful. */
   return (char *) file;
--- a/src/warc.c	2026-10-04 07:44:00.915903879 +0100
+++ b/src/warc.c	2026-10-04 07:44:14.015797342 +0100
@@ -43,6 +43,9 @@
 #include <sha1.h>
 #include <base32.h>
 #include <unistd.h>
+#ifdef __VMS
+# include "vms.h"
+#endif /* def __VMS */
 #ifdef HAVE_LIBZ
 #include <zlib.h>
 #endif
